- [ ] add basic rhythme and freq judging
  - when judging turned on, create a sound stream for real time input
  - only show the judging result on burst detected, which means don't judge the missed notes
  - find the nearest note when burst is heard, and show color which ranges from green to light
  - by default the final score is computed by the weighted rhythme difference and freq difference
  - user can adjust the weight that rhythme difference contributes to the result and freq difference
    contributes to the result in the settings
  - do not show the numbered score, but store the result for further usage

- [ ] generate song automatically
  - use Magenta.js (Google, runs in browser via TensorFlow.js) for ML-based melody generation
  - models: MusicRNN (seed + continue), MusicVAE (free-form sampling), MelodyRNN (full melody from scratch)
  - output is NoteSequence (MIDI pitch + start/end times) → convert to scale degrees relative to song key → emit .mmd
  - generated songs plug into existing quiz engine
  - note: model weights are ~20MB; MusicVAE is slow on CPU


